# What the test did, in committed slots:
#   slot 1  JobOp::Register(settle-auction)
#   slot 2  JobOp::Claim(worker-a)  \ proposed concurrently from node 1 and
#   slot 3  JobOp::Claim(worker-b)  / node 2; one applies, one is refused
#   slot 4  JobOp::Fire(expected epoch 1, generation 2) -> refused (no fence 2)
#   slot 5  JobOp::Fire(expected epoch 1, generation 1) -> fires the job
#
# Assertions:
#   - all three process replicas report the same `job` state and digest
#   - the job is held by exactly one worker and the fence generation is 1
#     (a second claim did not issue a fence)
#   - slot 4 is committed but leaves the job claimed
#   - slot 5 moves the job to fired
